node_modules/
release/
dist/

# ---- Reference material, not part of the build ----
# Screenshots of real apps, kept only as design reference. They're large and
# they're other people's artwork, so they stay out of the repo and out of the
# package (electron-builder excludes /appicons/ too).
#
# Nothing in the build reads them any more. There used to be an importer that
# turned these straight into the shipped home-screen icons, which meant the
# committed tiles in assets/icons were resampled copies of real logos. That is
# gone: every icon is now drawn from primitives in tools/icon-specs.js, and
# every product in the collection is fictional (tools/brand-map.js). Please
# don't reintroduce a path from this folder to assets/.
/appicons/
/appstore screenshots/
/apple healthj/
/cashappss/
/insta/
/kalshi/
/venmo/
/whop/
/IMG_*.png
/x.jpg

# ---- Local ----
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The design backlog. Useful precisely because it names the real products
# whose layouts are worth studying — "Revolut" tells you what to go and
# look at in a way "colourful multi-currency neobank" does not. That is
# also exactly why it does not belong in a public repo: nothing shipped
# from this list infringes anything, but a committed to-do list of real
# companies to rebuild reads like intent to, and it would be the first
# thing quoted back at you. Keep it, keep it local.
/IDEAS.md

# NOTE: assets/icons, assets/manifests, assets/coins, assets/appstore,
# resources/krypt.* and build/icon.png are deliberately committed. They are
# generated by `npm run icons` / `npm run art`, which now need no inputs at
# all — committing the output just keeps packaging reproducible and lets you
# see in a diff when a mark changes.
